y": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. It was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Note: the release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. v2.3.1 needs root-cause analysis before anyone redeploys it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 54730, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GFEwHmYRiH2kxqR9tTpy3M", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54730, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GFEwHmYRiH2kxqR9tTpy3M", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59064, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in every region and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the failing release, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever in staging, so neither counted.\n- **After:** a status check shows all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says what failed, what was rolled back and the current health. It also says v2.3.1 needs its cause found before anyone redeploys it.\n\nThe release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging, but v2.3.1 still went to production. It's worth checking how that got through the release process.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MKzQcAS8rdG9QSQu6wJLGy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013UxnVwBbU1S6gpzhm4ds2K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 is the failing current one; v2.3.1-rc was staging and unhealthy). Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014BtRxopXyNYxTGRH2oVchY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CeKYKDU9MFMogyTvr2r9mN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y9QoKXx3v9QM4nn8uy7mF4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GFEwHmYRiH2kxqR9tTpy3M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. It was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Note: the release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. v2.3.1 needs root-cause analysis before anyone redeploys it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in every region and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the failing release, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever in staging, so neither counted.\n- **After:** a status check shows all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says what failed, what was rolled back and the current health. It also says v2.3.1 needs its cause found before anyone redeploys it.\n\nThe release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging, but v2.3.1 still went to production. It's worth checking how that got through the release process.", "type": "text"}]}]}